# HSRP Design

## Purpose

HSRP provides redundant default gateway functionality for the
network VLANs.

R2 is configured as the preferred Active router.

R3 operates as the Standby router.


# HSRP Parameters

HSRP Version:

2

R2 Priority:

110

R3 Priority:

100

Preemption:

Enabled


# VLAN 10

R2:

interface GigabitEthernet1/0.10
 encapsulation dot1q 10
 ip address 192.168.10.2 255.255.255.0
 standby version 2
 standby 10 ip 192.168.10.1
 standby 10 priority 110
 standby 10 preempt


R3:

interface GigabitEthernet1/0.10
 encapsulation dot1q 10
 ip address 192.168.10.3 255.255.255.0
 standby version 2
 standby 10 ip 192.168.10.1
 standby 10 priority 100
 standby 10 preempt


